          %h1#contents Contents
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#properties"} Properties
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#RelationToComplexKTheory"} Relation to complex K-theory
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#RelationToTateKTheory"} Relation to Tate K-theory
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#relation_to_the_witten_genus"} Relation to the Witten genus
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"} Related concepts
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em Tate curve
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+neighbourhood"} formal neighbourhood
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nodal+curve"} nodal curve
            inside the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactification"} compactified
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack+of+elliptic+curves"} moduli stack of elliptic curves
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℳ
                      %mover
                        %mi ell
                        %mo ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}_{\overline{ell}}
          %p
            Over a given base ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            it is an elliptic curve over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+series"} power series
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R [ [ q ] ]
            which may be thought of as the quotient of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multiplicative+group"} multiplicative group
            by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi q
                      %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q^{\mathbb{Z}}
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#RelationToComplexKTheory Relation to complex K-theory
          %p
            The Tate curve is naturally an
            %span.newWikiWord
              oriented elliptic curve
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/oriented+elliptic+curve"} ?
            and as such classified by a map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spec
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mi KU
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo )
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msup
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mi Der
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Spec \left(  KU ( ( q ) ) \right) \longrightarrow \mathcal{M}^{Der}
          %p
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+algebraic+geometry"} derived algebraic geometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+series"} power series
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KU"} KU
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E+ring"} E-∞ ring
            to the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+moduli+stack+of+derived+elliptic+curves"} derived moduli stack of derived elliptic curves
          %h3#RelationToTateKTheory Relation to Tate K-theory
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+cohomology+theory"} generalized cohomology theory
            over the Tate curve by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Goerss-Hopkins-Miller+theorem"} Goerss-Hopkins-Miller theorem
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tate+K-theory"} Tate K-theory
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi KO
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} KO[ [q] ]
          %p
            This is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+limit"} homotopy limit
            over copies
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi KO
                  %mo ∧
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi q
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi q
                    %mi n
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo +
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} KO \wedge \{1, q, \cdots, q^n\}_+
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KO"} KO
            with formal parameters adjoined.
          %h3#relation_to_the_witten_genus Relation to the Witten genus
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+genus"} elliptic genus
            associated with the Tate curve is, according to the
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#RelationToComplexKTheory"} above
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+power+series"} formal power series
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory"} K-theory
            classes. This is the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witten+genus"} Witten genus
            (
            %a{:href => "#Hopkins94"}> Hopkins 94
            ).
          %p
            Physically, Witten obtained this as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partition+function"} partition function
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string"} heterotic string
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbation+theory"} perturbation theory
            about configurations where all the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldsheet"} worldsheet
            sits in a single point of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+space"} target space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldsheet"} worldsheet
            is the Tate curve.
          %p
            Formally this is given by the homotopy groups of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/String+orientation+of+tmf"} String orientation of tmf
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mi String
                  %mo →
                  %mi tmf
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M String \to tmf
            followed by the map to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tate+K-theory"} Tate K-theory
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#RelationToTateKTheory"} above
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "tmf#MapToTateKTheory"} here
